 "transcript": [
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Why do you not come in to your father and eat a little food?\"",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"We have been to the officer's house, father, and the young ladies have given us many gifts, and they are to be married to us, and we have been to the rich men's houses and have feasted and danced and sung and played and have been in the moonlight and have eaten a good meal and have danced and played and been merry and drunk and have come home.\"",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung enters, sees his sons",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung scolds eldest son",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Now I would go to my land and I would go out into the fields and I would eat the food I have grown and I would sleep on the earth, and I would not have these two young dogs in my house forever eating my silver and gold.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung enters, sees his sons",
  "[action] The eldest son watches Wang Lung closely.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Have you not eaten a little food and drunk a little drink and been a little merry?\"",
